<section class="panel-white">
  <div class="section max-w-3xl text-center">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-medium text-al-navy sm:text-4xl">The Industry Reality</h2>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-al-ink/75">Elite performance pushes a horse’s body to its physiological limits. When oxygen demand outpaces supply, a predictable cascade of performance-limiting events begins—reducing speed, increasing injury risk, and shortening careers.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel-grey">
  <div class="section">
    <h2 class="font-display text-center text-2xl font-medium text-al-navy sm:text-3xl">Phases of Performance Decline in an 8 Furlong Race</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-center text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-red-600">Due to Insufficient Oxygen to the Muscles</p>
    <div class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-al-line bg-white">
      <img src="/images/racing/cascade-chart.jpg" alt="Phases of performance decline cascade chart" class="w-full object-contain" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel-white">
  <div class="section max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="font-display text-center text-3xl font-medium text-al-navy">The Effects</h2>
    <ul class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-sm text-al-ink/80">
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-semibold text-al-orange">70–80%</span> of racehorses experience Exercise-Induced Pulmonary Hemorrhage (EIPH) at some point in their careers.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-semibold text-al-orange">80–90%</span> show musculoskeletal stress markers linked to repeated high-intensity work.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-semibold text-al-orange">Premature retirement</span> often follows unresolved oxygen debt, inflammation, and recovery failure.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-semibold text-al-orange">Catastrophic injury risk</span> rises when physiological balance breaks down under peak load.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel-grey">
